#basePath	Day2

:: BeginDay
@trigger    SceneReady
@boostScore 100
@cutscene
@who    Astrid

$call InitUpdateMasks()
$call EnableDocumentClose("HerculesPostcard", false)
$call EnableDocumentClose("1833", false)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(CoordinateInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(PhotometerInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(BlueWavelength, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(ColorInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(TemperatureInstrument, true)
$call SpawnDocument("MiniLabors")

$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call StopOpenMode()
$call SetInputState(true)
$call MoveToView("DocumentPuzzle")

{@Astrid} Looks like I got some mail... At least the mail service is still working... $[Day2/Astrid/l2_a_1]
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 40)
$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("Day2DadIcecubePostcard")
{@Astrid} Wow... I wonder if he ever feels weird about the auroras there. I think it might freak me out. $[Day2/Astrid/l2d_a_1]
{@Astrid} Dad said he sent this just a few weeks ago. 

:: SpawnPuzzleDocs1
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "Day2DadIcecubePostcard"
@cutscene
@interrupt
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call Wait(1)
{@Astrid} Elijah! Finally, some news. $[Day2/Astrid/l2_a_2]
$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("HerculesPostcard")
{@Astrid} I love his postcards. Must be traveling with his art supplies as always. Looks like the Hercules constellation? 
$call SetInputState(true)
$call QueueMusic("Music.StarDome", 3)

:: FlipHercules
@trigger    DocumentInspectFlip
@when   documentId == "HerculesPostcard"
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

{@Astrid} Oh Elijah... Is it safe traveling out there on your own? And what do you mean about the end of the world?
{@Astrid} What is going to fall apart? Elijah...why with the riddles? I wish you would just say what you mean. 
$call EnableDocumentClose("HerculesPostcard", true, true)

:: SpawnPuzzleDocs2
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "HerculesPostcard"
@cutscene
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call Wait(1)
$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("Day2Martha")
{@Astrid} I feel so guilty for leaving Aunt Martha to run the clinic. She really relied on me. 
$call SetInputState(true)

:: InspectMiniMap
@trigger    DocumentInspectStart
@when   documentId == "MiniLabors"
@once

{@Astrid} Hmmm, the Twelve Labor's of Hercules... Didn't Elijah say something about this in his letter?
{@Astrid} I bet he is at one of these stations. Or maybe on his way. I hope he is safe. 

:: SpawnPuzzleDocs3
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "Day2Martha"
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call Wait(1)
$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("CouplePhoto")
{@Astrid} Oh! I love this!
$call SetInputState(true)

:: DocumentPuzzleStart
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "CouplePhoto"
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call Wait(1)
$call StartDocumentPuzzle("Day2DocumentPuzzle")
$call SetInputState(true)
{@Astrid} Where is Elijah? Is he okay? $[Day2/Astrid/l2_a_3]

:: IncorrectDocumentResponse1
@trigger    DocumentPuzzlePromptStart
@when documentId == "Day2DadIcecubePostcard"

{@Astrid} Elijah in Antarctica...? No, that wouldn't make sense. 

:: IncorrectDocumentResponse2
@trigger    DocumentPuzzlePromptStart
@when documentId == "HerculesPostcard"

{@Astrid} Staying at Aunt Martha's to help out? They would drive each other crazy. That's not it? $[Day2/Astrid/l2d_a_4]

:: CorrectDocumentResponse
@trigger    DocumentPuzzlePromptStart
@when documentId == "MiniLabors"
@cutscene
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
{@Astrid} That's it. Elijah left Aunt Martha's and is back on the road now headed to one of these stations.
$call Wait(1)
$call MoveToView("Desk")
$call Wait(1)

$call MoveToView("Right")
{@Radio} CERES HQ to Station Twelve.
{@Radio} IceCube is reading a high-energy neutrino emission from the area of the Hydra Constellation. 
{@Radio} Identification of nearby celestial objects is requested. Uploading area of interest.
$call WaitForMovedToView("Monitor")
$call MonitorUI->PlayRadioDownload(4)
$call StartNeutrinoNavigation()
$call SetInputState(true)

:: NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@trigger    NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@cutscene
@once

$call StopNeutrinoNavigation()
$call StartOpenMode()
{@Radio} We need to know the spectral types of these stars. In order to determine that you’ll need to calculate the temperature.
{@Radio} Select a star on your teescope monitor.
$set temp:waitingForNeutrinoStar = true

:: OnStarSelected
@trigger    OnNeutrinoStarSelected
@when   temp:waitingForNeutrinoStar
@cutscene
@interrupt
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
{@Radio} Great. Now you’ll need to capture the same data in the blue wavelength.
{@Radio} Select the blue wavelength filter
$set temp:waitingForBlueFilter = true
$call LockMonitorFocus()
$call SetInputState(true)

:: BlueFilterSelected
@trigger OnLabInteraction
@when actorId == "BlueFilter", temp:waitingForBlueFilter
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$set temp:waitingForBlueFilter = false
{@Radio} Now you just need to use that temperature to look up the spectral type in your reference guide.
{@Radio} Look up the spectral type in your manual, and submit the data.

:: PointsUpdated0
@trigger    PointsUpdated
@when   sciencePoints > 0
@cutscene
@once

$call UnlockMonitorFocus()
{@Radio} Nice Job, You're getting the hang of this.

:: PointsUpdated
@trigger    PointsUpdated
@when   sciencePoints > 2
@cutscene
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call SetRefGuideActive(false)

$call Wait(3)

$call StopOpenMode()
$call ClearMonitorSelection()

$call MonitorUI->PlayRadioDownload(2)
$call Wait(1)
$call MonitorUI->ShowCeresLogo():wait
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(SpectrometerInstrument, true)
{@Radio} Congratulations on being awarded clearance level 3. You are now cleared to use the spectrometer.
{@Radio} Please reference your CERES Operator Manual for further information about your equipment.  $[Day2/Radio/l1_r_3(2)]
{@Radio} Thanking you for being an important part of the CERES Distributed Network of Citizen Observatories. Together, we will map the stars for a better tomorrow. $[Day2/Radio/l1_r_3(3)]
$call MonitorUI->HideCeresLogo()

$call MoveToView("Left")
{@Astrid} Hmmm, Hercules. Just like Elijah's postcard. 
$call MoveToView("Right")
{@Astrid} These are the puzzles Elijah had been working on. What is this all for? 
// $set temp:waitingForRefGuidePuzzle = true

// :: HerculesPuzzleRef
// @trigger    OnRefGuideOpened
// @when   temp:waitingForRefGuidePuzzle
// @boostScore 300
// @interrupt
// @cutscene
// @once

// $set temp:waitingForRefGuidePuzzle = false
//TODO
$call OpenRefGuidePage("DataTransfer")
(*typing sounds*)
$call Wait(1)
$call StartPuzzleNavigation()
$call SetInputState(true)

:: PuzzleNavigationComplete
@trigger    PuzzleNavigationComplete
@cutscene
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call StopPuzzleNavigation()
$call SetRefGuideActive(false)
$call ClearMonitorSelection()
$call Wait(1)
$call StartPuzzleMode()
$call SetInputState(true)

:: HerculesPuzzleComplete
@trigger    CorrectPuzzleSubmission
@when   puzzleName == "Hercules"
@cutscene
@once

$call ClearMonitorSelection()
$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call SetInputState(false)
{@Elijah} If you’re hearing this, it means you’ve solved Hercules—and that part of the satellite could come back online soon. 
{@Elijah} That would be huge. With historical data restored, the other astronomers can finally start seeing the bigger picture.
{@Elijah} I knew you’d get this far. Keep going. Everything depends on it now.

{@Dad} Astrid... What are you up to? Elijahs puzzles are a wild goose chase. I don't want you getting your hopes up. 

{@Astrid} But dad, I think I'm getting close here...
{@Astrid} That satellite was built to withstand a CME. If we could decrypt what's stored on it... it would change everything.

{@Dad} Its a lost cause is what it is. Time to focus on our mission. 

{@Astrid} It looks like each of these puzzles reveals part of the password. I actually think I might be making progress here.

{@Dad} The guy who built the satellite was... eccentric putting it mildly. 
{@Dad} Even if Elijah could have solved it, who knows if it would have worked. 

{@Astrid} Ugh. But Elijah's notes said we might be too late. Too late for what?

{@Monitor} Warning. Station Twelve. You have been flagged non-compliant. You will lose access to this frequency upon any further violation.
{@Monitor} I advise that you review communication protocols if you want to avoid termination. 
{@Monitor} Remember, commnication is a privilege, not a right. 

{@Dad} Astrid, please. Focus on the task at hand. I don't want to get cut off ... frustrated sigh, centering himself
//Please tune radio to 375 mhz...
{@Dad} You got your next access level. Stay on target. G'night Little Bear.

{@Astrid} Whoa… what's this picture? It must have fallen out of the reference guide?

$set temp:d3PostcardRead = false
$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("1833")
$call SetInputState(true)

:: Flip1833
@trigger    DocumentInspectFlip
@when   documentId == "1833"
@cutscene
@interrupt
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
{@Astrid} The 1833 Leonid Meteor Storm... I’ve never heard of this before.
{@Astrid} It looks like the sky was completely filled with meteors—not just a few streaks, but thousands. Like the whole sky was breaking apart.
{@Astrid} People must have thought the world was ending.... wait...
{@Astrid} Does he think it’s going to happen again? Is that what he has been hinting at? 
{@Astrid} If this is true, people won’t understand what’s happening. Everyone’s gonna panic. 
{@Astrid} It would look like the sky is falling - the end of the world.
{@Astrid} Oh God. Things are just starting to get better. 
{@Astrid} If something like this hit now… it’d be worse. So much worse.
{@Astrid} I feel pretty safe up here at the edge of nowhere. It would be nice if I wasn't totally alone. 
{@Astrid} Maybe I could write to the newspaper and tell people what’s happening?
{@Astrid} Sigh. but I guess I would need to know what is actually happening.
{@Astrid} When and where is this meteor storm coming?
{@Astrid} Elijah! What have you gotten us into?
$set temp:d3PostcardRead = true
$call EnableDocumentClose("1833", true, true)
$call SetInputState(true)

:: End1833
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "1833", temp:d3PostcardRead
@interrupt
@once

$call LoadNextDay()